, which serves as a demonstration of an exercise aimed at improving muscle tone and mobility of the soft palate. Together, these elements illustrate both culinary and physical activities, emphasizing the importance of tools in food preparation and exercises for enhancing oral muscle function.", "HOSPITALARIA:HOSPITALARIA refers to the context of hospital settings where specific recipes and guidelines for managing dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing, are applied. Additionally, it encompasses a medical event that took place over a period of three days, focusing on preoperative nutrition. This event highlights the importance of nutritional management in hospital care, particularly in relation to patients who may have difficulties with swallowing.", "MINISTERIO DE SANIDAD, SERVICIOS SOCIALES E IGUALDAD:The \"Ministerio de Sanidad, Servicios Sociales e Igualdad\" is a governmental body in Spain responsible for the formulation and implementation of health and social services policies. This ministry oversees public health initiatives and is tasked with developing health-related strategies, including those focused on nutrition and clinical practice guidelines. Its role encompasses a broad spectrum of responsibilities aimed at promoting health and well-being within the Spanish population, ensuring that effective health policies and social services are in place to support the community.", "UNIVERSIDAD COMPLUTENSE:The Universidad Complutense is a public university located in Madrid, Spain, recognized for its research and educational programs across a wide range of disciplines, including medicine. It is notable for its academic contributions and has a diverse faculty, including Pilar Matía Martín, who serves as an associate professor at the institution.", "COMISIÓN EUROPEA:The Comisión Europea, also known as the European Commission, is the executive body of the European Union. It plays a crucial role in proposing legislation and implementing decisions within the EU framework. Recently, the Comisión Europea presented a report to the European Parliament and Council concerning foods intended for athletes. Additionally, it is responsible for ensuring that food labeling regulations are updated and enforced, highlighting its commitment to maintaining food safety and transparency in the market.", "AGENCIA DE CALIDAD SANITARIA DE ANDALUCÍA:The AGENCIA DE CALIDAD SANITARIA DE ANDALUCÍA, also known as the Agency for Health Quality in Andalusia (ACSA), is an institution dedicated to ensuring the quality of health services within the Andalusian region of Spain. In addition to its primary role in overseeing health service quality, the agency is also responsible for reviewing and accrediting health-related web content in Spain, thereby contributing to the overall improvement and reliability of health information available to the public.", "ORGANIZACIÓN PANAMERICANA DE LA SALUD:The Pan American Health Organization is an international public health agency working to improve health and living standards in the Americas.", "HACCP:HACCP (Hazard Analysis and Critical Control Points) is a systematic preventive approach to food safety that addresses physical, chemical, and biological hazards.", "GONZÁLEZ CALLEJAS MJ:González Callejas MJ is an author who wrote about food safety management in hospital kitchens.", "CARACUEL GARCÍA A:Caracuel García A is an author who contributed to the standardization of hospital food.", "FERRER SVODODA C:Ferrer Svododa C is an author who wrote about hygiene and food safety standards in clinical nutrition.", "CALLEJA-FERNÁNDEZ A:Calleja-Fernández A is a researcher who studied the impact of kitchen organization on malnourished inpatients.", "HERRERA ÚBEDA MA:", "PILAR GALLEGO IQUIERDO:Pilar Gallego Izquierdo is a co-author focused on the rehabilitation techniques for oropharyngeal dysphagia.", "EUROPEAN PARLIAMENT:The European Parliament is involved in regulations regarding food information provided to consumers."], "par